Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:06.00,Default,,0,0,0,,zombieSatellite brings forgotten spacecraft into a hands-on mobile experience.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.00,0:00:12.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Find the next pass, point your phone, and follow the computed Doppler shift.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.00,0:00:17.50,Default,,0,0,0,,The archive connects each spacecraft to its documented history.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.50,0:00:23.00,Default,,0,0,0,,IMAGE was rediscovered in 2018 by radio amateur Scott Tilley.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.00,0:00:29.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The AR view places the calculated satellite direction over the phone camera.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.00,0:00:35.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Switch satellites to explore their different positions in the sky.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.00,0:00:42.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The sky view keeps the orbit geometry visible without the camera backdrop.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.00,0:00:49.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Direction cues help you find an object even when it is outside the view.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.00,0:00:54.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Pass predictions use public orbital data and the observer location.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.00,0:00:59.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Choose a satellite, open its session, and start the 60x demo.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.00,0:01:05.00,Default,,0,0,0,,This is demo mode with auto-point: a predicted pass played at 60x speed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.00,0:01:10.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Follow the pointing lock and watch the Doppler readout change through the pass.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.00,0:01:15.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The beacon tone is simulated. The phone receives no satellite radio signal.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.00,0:01:21.00,Default,,0,0,0,,At the end of the pass, review the session and open your QSL collection.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.00,0:01:26.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Each completed session produces a QSL card in the amateur radio tradition.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.00,0:01:31.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The cards are labelled as simulated sessions, not proof of real reception.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.00,0:01:37.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Kiro development is documented in eleven feature specs and two steering files.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.00,0:01:43.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The specs cover orbit prediction, pointing, sessions, QSL cards and the app shell.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.00,0:01:51.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Try zombieSatellite: find a pass, point your phone, and follow the orbit.